 "profile": "replay-log-format",
 "question": "Question: what minimal event record makes a run replayable such that replaying it reproduces the SAME plan and the SAME verdicts without re-dispatching? Target: specify and implement that record. Acceptance: replay of a recorded run produces a byte-identical plan and identical oracle verdicts, with zero spawns.",
 "replay_log_format": {
  "answer": "The minimal record is a six-kind JSONL stream whose planning inputs are hashed and whose plan is a function of those inputs. Replay is recompute-plus-reapply, not re-dispatch.",
  "clock": "FrozenClock logical ticks only. Wall-clock, timezone, uuid4 and time.time must not enter the plan bytes.",
  "encoding": "UTF-8 JSONL, LF-only, canonical dumps (sort_keys, separators comma-colon)",
  "envelope_required": [
   "v",
   "seq",
   "kind",
   "ts_logical",
   "run_id",
   "payload"
  ],
  "kinds_closed": [
   "run.start",
   "plan.input",
   "unit.planned",
   "dispatch.recorded",
   "oracle.verdict",
   "run.end"
  ],
  "load_bearing_fields": [
   "run.start.payload.workflow",
   "run.start.payload.params",
   "plan.input.payload.value (fan-out items)",
   "plan.input.payload.value_hash",
   "oracle.verdict.payload.verdict",
   "oracle.verdict.payload.receipt_sha256",
   "run.end.payload.plan_sha256"
  ],
  "non_load_bearing_fields": [
   "debug_note",
   "note",
   "annotation"
  ],
  "reconstruction": "Replay recomputes the plan from run.start.workflow + run.start.params + plan.input values (producer receipts). It re-applies oracle.verdict rows. It never calls the rail. unit.planned and dispatch.recorded are audit; they are not the reconstruction source, so dropping a planning input cannot be masked by a stored plan blob."
 },
